<header><p class="st-kicker">duchy · Germany and Central Europe</p><h1 class="st-title">Duchy of Znojmo</h1><p class="st-meta">1092 CE – 1200 CE (approx.) · capital Znojmo</p></header>
<p class="st-teaser">The southern Moravian appanage of the Přemyslid dynasty, centred on Znojmo, whose Romanesque rotunda preserves rare paintings of the Bohemian dukes.</p>
<div class="st-body"><div class="st-text"><h2>Origins</h2><p><a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/znojmo">Znojmo</a> in southern <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/empire/margraviate-of-moravia">Moravia</a> was split off from the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/brno">Brno</a> <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/appanage">appanage</a> around 1092, when Conrad I of Brno became Duke of <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/empire/kingdom-of-bohemia">Bohemia</a> and his son <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/litold-of-znojmo">Litold</a> received Znojmo. It was one of three Moravian appanages, alongside <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/olomouc">Olomouc</a> and Brno, held by junior <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/premyslid-dynasty">Přemyslid</a> princes.</p><h2>Rule and society</h2><p>The princes ruled from the castle of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/znojmo">Znojmo</a> on a crag above the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/thaya">Dyje</a> (Thaya) river, close to the Austrian border. The castle's <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/romanesque-architecture">Romanesque</a> rotunda of Saint Catherine contains wall paintings of 1134 showing the legendary and historical <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/premyslid-dynasty">Přemyslid</a> rulers, an important source for the dynasty's self-image. <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/conrad-ii-of-znojmo">Conrad II of Znojmo</a> was a strong contender for the Bohemian throne.</p><h2>Decline and legacy</h2><p>The <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/appanage">appanage</a> system ended in the late 12th century as <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/empire/margraviate-of-moravia">Moravia</a> became a margraviate; around 1197 <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/vladislaus-iii-duke-of-bohemia">Vladislaus Henry</a> united the Moravian lands. <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/znojmo">Znojmo</a> became a royal town in the 13th century under <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/ottokar-i-of-bohemia">Ottokar I</a>.</p></div><aside class="st-side"><div class="st-emblem" role="img" aria-label="duchy, 1092 CE – 1200 CE (approx.)"><svg viewBox="0 0 100 100" aria-hidden="true"><path d="M20 74 H80 V60 H20 Z"/><path d="M20 60 Q35 46 50 60 Q65 46 80 60"/><circle cx="20" cy="54" r="3"/><circle cx="35" cy="48" r="3"/><circle cx="50" cy="44" r="3"/><circle cx="65" cy="48" r="3"/><circle cx="80" cy="54" r="3"/></svg><p class="st-emblem-type">duchy</p><p class="st-emblem-region">Germany and Central Europe</p><div class="st-span" aria-hidden="true"><span class="st-span-bar" style="left:81.43%;width:2.15%"></span></div><div class="st-span-axis" aria-hidden="true"><span>3000 BCE</span><span>1 CE</span><span>2000</span></div></div><dl class="st-facts"><dt>Years</dt><dd>1092 CE – 1200 CE (approx.)</dd><dt>Centuries</dt><dd><a href="/centuries/11th-century">11th century</a> – <a href="/centuries/13th-century">13th century</a></dd><dt>Type</dt><dd>duchy</dd><dt>Character</dt><dd>feudal</dd><dt>Capital</dt><dd>Znojmo</dd><dt>Rulers</dt><dd>Litold of Znojmo, Conrad II of Znojmo</dd><dt>Religion</dt><dd>Catholic Christianity</dd><dt>Language</dt><dd>Old Czech</dd><dt>Today</dt><dd><a href="/countries/czech-republic">Czech Republic</a></dd><dt>Also</dt><dd>Znaim, Moravian appanage of Znojmo</dd></dl><figure class="st-locator"><a href="/atlas?year=1146&amp;focus=duchy-of-znojmo" aria-label="Duchy of Znojmo on the atlas"><svg class="map map-loc" viewBox="5051 472 640 512" role="img" aria-label="Map: where Duchy of Znojmo lay"><image href="/maps/world.svg" x="0" y="0" width="10000" height="4393"/><path class="map-tie" d="M5371 728L5330 692M5371 728L5383 718"/><path class="map-dot-n" d="M5330 692h0M5383 718h0"/><path class="map-dot-halo" d="M5371 728h0"/><path class="map-dot-me" d="M5371 728h0"/></svg></a><figcaption>The dot marks Znojmo. <a href="/atlas?year=1146&amp;focus=duchy-of-znojmo">On the atlas &rarr;</a></figcaption></figure></aside></div>
